  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 103 PM EDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\nThe spell of 70+ degree temps has ended for the time being, with the \nairmass behind yesterday's cold front shaving off about 10 degrees \nin high temps going into the weekend (low to mid 60s, maybe a few \nupper 60s by Monday). Drier low levels remain in place with \ndewpoints in the 40s and surrounding soundings shows fairly dry\nconditions below 850 mb. Hi-res models continue to show some \nspurious light showers/sprinkles for later this afternoon into \nSat afternoon as an elevated warm front attempts to work north \ntowards the region. 295-305K isentropic surfaces show decent \nlift and low CPDs, but then impacts of dry air below that leads \nto a lower confidence forecast on measurable precip. Northern \nareas will be on the edge of the RRQ of a 90 kt jet streak which\nmay help give a little more kick to the lift. Model blend has \nbacked off on timing of arrival overnight with differences in \nmodels on where and when some light shower activity could take \nshape with some indications of a diurnal uptick by the HRRR/RAP \nin the afternoon. Will continue with no more than chc pops into \nSaturday afternoon with best chances on Saturday. Hopefully, \nwhatever is around will be gone by the time trick or treaters \nhit the streets. \n\nTrough currently moving onshore in S California will move northeast \nin a weakened state, but will enough lift to bring another chance \nfor showers Sunday afternoon, possibly lingering into Monday. \nThereafter, the deeper trough that has been discussed at length for \ndays will become the main challenge through much of the upcoming \nweek with focus on mid week. Energy is still on the edge of the best \nupper air sampling, but hopefully better agreement starts over the \nweekend into early next week as it moves east. Best signals still \npoint towards mid week being on the wetter side, but the main upper \nlow may remain SW of the area. While severe weather threat may be \nlow, still expected one or more rounds of precip. The active pattern \nwill likely persist into next weekend, but low confidence exists \ngiven the plethora of differences in models.",
